RoCE one-shot all-reduce for TP=2 decode-size messages, via b12x's RoCEnante (contributed by @sethforprivacy).
- NCCL's ring LL takes 38-93 us per decode-size all-reduce on two GB10s. b12x.comm.roce (local-inference-lab/b12x
  @ e4084d2e, Apache-2.0) RDMA-writes each rank's input into pinned host slots on the peer (no GPUDirect on GB10) and
  one kernel sums in a fixed rank order: ~15 us. TP=2 messages up to ROCE_AR_MAX bytes (default 1 MiB; bf16/fp16/fp32,
  contiguous, 16-byte multiple) take it, in eager mode and inside CUDA graphs; larger ones stay on NCCL. The routing
  decision is made from shape and dtype only, so both ranks always route alike.
- Exact: with two ranks there is one pair of values to add and both ranks sum in the same order. Stress test of
  360,000 all-reduces inside a captured CUDA graph (5 KB-1 MB, inputs rotated every replay): every output
  bit-identical to NCCL's sum, 0 stale results, outputs identical across ranks.
- Fail-stop: a timed-out RDMA wait freezes the runtime and the next eager step raises (check_health() in the logits
  all-gather), so a dead link ends the engine like an NCCL timeout instead of hanging.
- Measured on 2x GB10, image v6, hibrid48, K=5, together with dual-rail NCCL (NCCL_IB_HCA= both PCIe halves +
  NCCL_IB_MERGE_NICS=1): 1-stream decode step -1.9 ms, 8 / 16 streams +6 / +5 %, NLL unchanged, 0 RoCE errors; in
  production on our pair since 2026-10-01.
- Needs, on BOTH boxes: b12x at e4084d2e under the cache dir (it is mounted at /cache), e.g.
  `git clone https://github.com/local-inference-lab/b12x cache/b12x && git -C cache/b12x checkout e4084d2e`, and
  in recipe.yaml env: ROCE_AR: "1", PYTHONPATH: "/cache/b12x". Devices: ROCE_AR_HCAS, else this box's NCCL_IB_HCA
  (run.sh sets it per box). We run it with both PCIe functions of the cabled port (e.g. rocep1s0f0,roceP2p1s0f0),
  which needs the second function addressed on its own subnet; one HCA per box has not been measured.
- Startup logs "ROCE_AR: RoCEnante 2-rank all-reduce active (rank N, <hcas>, max <bytes> bytes)" on each rank.
  Without ROCE_AR=1 the patch does nothing (and b12x is not imported).

